> Equal logits average the values

A zero query and two zero keys give attention(.5,.5). Values2 and4 therefore produce3. This hand calculation checks the native plain attention path without relying on a trained network.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/scaled_dot_attention_worked.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace n=dm::nn;namespace m=n::models;std::filesystem::create_directories("build");n::AttentionOptions o;o.need_weights=true;o.impl=n::AttentionImpl::Plain;auto path=n::scaled_dot_product_attention(n::zeros({1,1,1}),n::zeros({1,2,1}),n::from_vector(std::vector<float>{2,4},{1,2,1}),o);auto values=n::concat({path.weights.reshape({2}),path.output.reshape({1})},0);if(path.output.item()!=3)return 1;
std::print("| coordinate | computed value |\n|---:|---:|\n");auto v=values.to_vector<double>();for(size_t i=0;i<v.size();++i)std::print("| {} | {:.9f} |\n",i,v[i]);n::save_npz("build/scaled_dot_attention_worked.npz",{{"values",values}});dm::graphics::RPlot::create().bars(n::arange(0,std::int64_t(v.size())).to_vector<double>(),v,"native values",{37,99,235}).title("Equal logits average the values").size(1000,550).save_svg("build/scaled_dot_attention_worked.svg");}
```
